{title: Grace Upon Your Lips}
{subtitle: Psalms 45:2}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]My heart stirs with a [Eb]noble [Bb]theme
I recite my vers[F]es for the king
[Gm]My tongue is the [Bb/D]pen of a [Eb]skilled [Gm]scribe
[Eb]Writing out what the spirit [Bb]sings
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are the fairest of men
Grace is poured [Gm]upon your lips
Therefore God [Eb]has blessed you forever
Your beauty [F]outshines all others
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Strap your sword to your [Eb]side
O [Gm]mighty one in glory and [F]majesty
[Bb]Ride out in [Bb/D]triumph for [Eb]truth
Let [Gm]righteousness [F]guide your [Bb]destiny
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are the fairest of men
Grace is [Gm]poured upon your lips
Therefore God [Eb]has blessed you forever
Your beauty [F]outshines all others
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Let your right hand reveal [Gm]awesome deeds
[Bb]In the cause of truth and hu[F]mility
[Eb]Your majesty rides out [Gm]in victory
A [Bb]skilled scribe’s pen for the [F]king
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You are the fai[Bb]rest of men
Grace is [Gm]poured upon your lips
Therefore God [Eb]has blessed you forever
Your beauty [F]outshines all others [Bb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Grace is [Gm]poured upon your lips
Blessed you forev[Eb]er
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [F] | [F] |
| [Bb] | [Eb] | [Bb] | [Eb] |
